2026-09-16T04:31:47.6219943Z       "body": "## Description\r\n\r\nFixes #11215.\r\n\r\nWhen `BackgroundTasks` are injected through FastAPI dependencies or path operations, they can be silently discarded when the endpoint returns a custom `Response` that already has a background task attached.\r\n\r\nThis change merges the injected background tasks with the background task already attached to the response instead of dropping the injected tasks.\r\n\r\nThe merge is applied to both relevant response-handling paths:\r\n\r\n* `get_request_handler`\r\n* `_FrontendRouteGroup.handle`\r\n\r\nThe regression tests cover:\r\n\r\n* Injected tasks with a single `BackgroundTask`\r\n* Injected tasks with a `BackgroundTasks` collection\r\n* Reusing the same `BackgroundTasks` instance\r\n* Dependency-only background tasks\r\n* Dependency and endpoint background tasks together\r\n* Responses without injected background tasks\r\n* Injected tasks without an explicit response background\r\n* Mixed async and sync background tasks\r\n\r\nThe tests reproduce the issue on the main branch and pass with this change.\r\n",
